          "line": 949,
          "message": "The comment-aware backward-boundary lookup rescans the full PDF prefix for every real stream, allowing a bounded PDF with many streams to consume excessive CPU (OWASP A06:2025).",
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "CheckStreamLimits calls LastIndexOfPdfToken for each stream. The changed implementation scans from byte zero to that stream, even when the preceding object boundary is nearby.",
            "failureScenario": "A PDF within the 10,485,760-byte limit contains many small, valid stream objects. Each stream causes another scan of the growing prefix, producing quadratic CPU work during preflight before the worker starts. This creates a reachable denial-of-service risk (OWASP A06:2025)."
          }
        }
